From: ios-milanf-port (desk phase, 2026-10-25)
Subject: [PATCH] MILANF: give milanf the platform expert, and a table to find it in

iokit/conf/files.arm64 lists all nine Sweet* drivers as 'optional iokitcpp',
so they compile on every board, and each one is wrapped in

  #if defined(SWEET)      (or ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)

which on milanf makes nine empty translation units. That is why the milanf
kernel links: nothing is missing, everything is absent.

Fixing only the driver would not have been enough, and this is the part
worth reading twice. iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp wraps the whole
personality table in the same ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET guard, so milanf's
gIOKernelConfigTables is currently just the shared IOPanicPlatform entry.
A platform expert with no personality pointing at it is never instantiated,
so the kernel would have gone looking for an IOPlatformExpert and found
none. Both halves are needed, which is why they are one patch.

The table is not widened wholesale, it gets a milanf arm of its own with
exactly one personality. Widening it would name SweetCPU, SweetHIDButtons,
SweetHIDTouch, SweetBattery, AppleCLCD, AppleKeyStore, IOWatchdog and
IOCoreSurfaceRoot, none of which exist yet on this board, and each would
earn an IOKit "can't find class" at boot. They come back one driver at a
time, each with its board values checked and its own personality here.

SweetFramebuffer will be the awkward one: it carries 1080x2400 in its
geometry and needs milanf's 1080x2460 plus its own base. SweetBattery's
SPMI register addresses need checking against the PM6125 the milanf DTB
declares. SweetCPU is closer than it looks but will need a second
personality, because the milanf ADT names its cores qcom,kryo660 while the
table matches qcom,kryo470 - that is a match-string difference, not a code
difference, since its only SoC constant is PSCI CPU_ON (0xC4000003).

The IOLog strings keep their 'SWEET:' prefix on purpose - research/
check-platform.gdb matches 'platform expert registered' in the QEMU
platform test, and renaming output for cosmetics is not worth
re-validating that. The header comment and the processTopLevel comment are
prose, so those are made board-neutral.

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetPlatformExpert.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetPlatformExpert.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetPlatformExpert.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetPlatformExpert.cpp
@@ -1,11 +1,12 @@
 /*
- * Minimal device-tree platform expert for Redmi Note 10 Pro (sweet).
+ * Minimal device-tree platform expert for the Qualcomm dev boards
+ * (sweet / SM7150, milanf / SM6375).
  * Uses XNU's normal platform, power-domain and nub initialization. Hardware
  * interrupt and power-management services are supplied by separate drivers.
  */
 #include <pexpert/arm64/board_config.h>
 
-#if defined(SWEET)
+#if defined(SWEET) || defined(MILANF)
 #include <IOKit/IOPlatformExpert.h>
 #include <IOKit/IODeviceTreeSupport.h>
 #include <IOKit/IOLib.h>
@@ -51,8 +52,9 @@
 {
 	/*
 	 * The stock implementation requires an Apple NVRAM /options node.
-	 * SWEET has no NVRAM controller; publish real CPU/device nodes without
-	 * inventing one. createNubs adds the topology's logical CPU/cluster IDs.
+	 * Neither board has an NVRAM controller; publish real CPU/device nodes
+	 * without inventing one. createNubs adds the topology's logical
+	 * CPU/cluster IDs.
 	 */
 	IORegistryEntry *cpus = root->childFromPath("cpus", gIODTPlane);
 	if (cpus != NULL) {
@@ -79,4 +81,4 @@
  * "compatible" string and "model" (D22AP / iPhone10,3 in the ADT), which
  * is what the iPhone userland (MobileGestalt) expects.
  */
-#endif /* SWEET */
+#endif /* SWEET || MILANF */
diff --git a/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp b/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp
--- a/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp
+++ b/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp
@@ -82,6 +82,27 @@
     "     'IOProviderClass' = IOResources;"
     "     'IOMatchCategory' = SweetBattery;"
     "   },"
+#elif defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MILANF)
+    /*
+     * milanf gets the platform expert and nothing else, for now. Every
+     * other Sweet* driver is still an empty translation unit on this
+     * board, and a personality whose class does not exist only earns
+     * an IOKit "can't find class" line. They come back one at a time,
+     * each with its own board values and its own personality here.
+     *
+     * IONameMatch is "xiaomi,sweet" and that is deliberate, not a
+     * copy-paste slip: the milanf ADT root compatible list is
+     *   D22AP | iPhone10,3 | motorola,milanf | qcom,sm6375 |
+     *   xiaomi,sweet | AppleARM
+     * so the device impersonates a sweet for the userland's benefit
+     * and this match is what the ADT actually publishes.
+     */
+    "   {"
+    "     'IOClass'         = SweetPlatformExpert;"
+    "     'IOProviderClass' = IOPlatformExpertDevice;"
+    "     'IONameMatch'     = 'xiaomi,sweet';"
+    "     'IOProbeScore'    = 10000:32;"
+    "   },"
 #endif
     "   {"
     "     'IOClass'         = IOPanicPlatform;"
